natalia bryant is opening up about why  she decided not to play college  volleyball after her dad and sister died  the 18 year old model who is currently a  freshman at the university of southern  california gets candid in a new  interview with teen vogue about the  heartbreaking decision explaining that  she always wanted to play division 1  volleyball but that all came to a  screeching halt after her dad kobe  bryant and sister gianna along with  seven others died in a january 2020  helicopter crash on the way to a  basketball tournament natalia explains  quote i quit volleyball after the  accident because a lot was going on at  the time i knew i didn't love volleyball  as much as they loved basketball i'm  okay with that i just wanted to take a  break from it while being a college  athlete is no longer in the teenager's  plans natalia never questioned whether  she would continue her education due in  large part to her mom vanessa bryant  quote for my mom it was really important  for me to go through high school and get  my education especially complete college  too and while her mom encouraged her to  go to college it was her dad who helped  her realize she wanted to major in film  as a parent we want our kids to learn  the model explains that watching movies  was one way she and her dad spent time  together in fact natalya said that after  seeing star wars the rise of skywalker  in 2019 she asked her dad that night to  watch the whole franchise with her a  request he happily obliged quote he was  just letting me play my playlist and jam  out to taylor swift the whole ride back  and talk about star wars too it was so  much fun and all that echoes what  natalia said last week during an  interview with her modeling agency img  my dad and i would always watch like as  many movies as we can and we'd go on  like movie marathons and then we'd also  like analyze as many movies as we can  and we'd like talk about it for months  anywhere we go we just keep talking  about like different films and how like  it reminds us of like where we are oh my  gosh like that architecture reminds me  of like this piece from like this film  so it's just things like that it just  really inspired me and i was like i want  to do this like  forever she added that in 10 years she  wants to follow in kobe's footsteps and  win an oscar i'm not sure for what or  what  oscar category but i definitely think  that's on my list and i definitely i  want to make a film  that's like where i can incorporate  fashion in like those fashion aspects  and i think like combining like my two  passions like that's just amazing  i want to be able to do that the nba  star won an oscar in 2018 for best  animated short film for dear basketball  i did everything for you  because that's what you do when someone  makes you feel as alive as you've made  me feel like gianna when the nominations  came out  you know she told me she said see that  hard work makes the dream work  and though natalia says reflecting on  her dad's life is quote bittersweet it's  something she does often quote i love  talking about my dad i enjoy talking  about him more than it's sad for me it's  a philosophy she shares with her mom in  large part because of natalia's younger  sisters four-year-old bianca and  two-year-old capri quote for my little  sisters we're trying to keep that memory  for them and also just trying to  remember to live out every day the way  they would  you
 

